{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"My dearest Marie,\n\nThe day began early at the Imperial Library. I spent the morning with Raphael and Marcantonio, paying the usual modest sum to the attendants. The light here is distinct from Berlin’s; one must tip well to be left in peace. The weather cleared by afternoon, so I walked.\n\nI confess I am tired. The Viennese have a habit of lingering over meals that tests my patience. I dined on a simple soup and bread; it was adequate, if uninspired. I think of Karl’s lessons at home and the quiet of our study.\n\nI saw a performance earlier, though I do not speak well of the dancers. Eberle was there, but the German school seems to lack the true spirit of movement. It is all form without life. I shall not return.\n\nI write this by candlelight. The ink is thick, but my thoughts are clear. I am well, though the cold seeps in. Give my regards to the boys.\n\nYours,\nG.W.F. Hegel"}}],"created":1795219371,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":218,"prompt_tokens":1114,"total_tokens":1332,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-5gttYvBciCyrLq3Ot7JRgH0i2jEjgd6D","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":1114,"prompt_ms":1064.512,"prompt_per_token_ms":0.9555763016157989,"prompt_per_second":1046.4889075933386,"predicted_n":218,"predicted_ms":5134.77,"predicted_per_token_ms":23.662534562211984,"predicted_per_second":42.260899709237215}}